          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: حقيقة",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حقيقة — ḥaqīqa — \"a fact\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "هذه حقيقة لا يعرفها كثير من الناس. hādhihi ḥaqīqa lā yaʿrifuhā kathīr min an-nās. This is a fact that many people do not know."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "في الحقيقة, fī al-ḥaqīqa, in fact."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حقيقة (ḥaqīqa) is built on the native Arabic root ḥ-q-q, \"to be true, to be due\" (Lane). A ḥaqīqa is what is truly so: a fact, the truth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
